  {
    "text": "Yes. Ciprofloxacin is a potent inhibitor of CYP1A2, and theophylline is cleared principally via CYP1A2. Inhibiting this enzyme would reduce theophylline clearance and raise its serum concentrations. Because theophylline has a narrow therapeutic range (and is monitored in practice), elevated levels risk toxicity (e.g., seizures, arrhythmias), making this a clinically significant pharmacokinetic interaction. Dose reduction or alternative antibiotic is typically advised.\n\nMECHANISM: CYP1A2 inhibition by ciprofloxacin decreases theophylline clearance, increasing theophylline exposure\nFINAL ANSWER: YES",
